1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,810
Technology is developing by leaps and bounds.
科技正飞速发展。

2
00:00:03,810 --> 00:00:10,410
A gadget as small as a smartphone now has more processing power than rockets to the Moon once had.
如今一部小小的智能手机，其处理能力甚至超过了当年用于登月的火箭。

3
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:17,120
New tech brings many advantages, making our lives easier and opening up new opportunities.
新技术带来诸多益处，既让我们的生活变得更加便捷，也开拓了全新的发展机遇。

4
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:21,820
One piece of kit that’s been really taking off recently is the drone.
近年来，一种设备的热度持续攀升，那就是无人机。

5
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:30,720
This pilotless mini aircraft, originally developed for aerial photography and warfare, is now bringing us benefits closer to home.
这种无人驾驶的小型飞行器最初是为航空摄影和军事用途研发的，如今正为我们的日常生活带来实实在在的好处。

6
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:41,350
In the last few years, tech companies such as Amazon, Alphabet and Uber have promised us delivery drones – bringing goods to our doorsteps in a matter of minutes.
过去几年里，亚马逊、字母表公司和优步等科技企业都曾承诺推出配送无人机——能在短短几分钟内将商品送到我们家门口。

7
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:45,820
Progress in developing them has, however, been slow.
不过，这类无人机的研发进程却较为缓慢。

8
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:52,380
Drones are helping to connect with and enhance the lives of people in remote locations.
无人机正助力偏远地区的人们加强联系、改善生活。

9
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:59,720
In the UK, the Royal Mail wants a fleet of 500 drones to help deliver the mail to far-flung communities.
在英国，皇家邮政计划配备一支由500架无人机组成的机队，为偏远社区提供邮件配送服务。

10
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:09,020
Windracers, the company developing the drones, say they can fly in fog and produce 30% fewer emissions than comparable piloted aircraft.
负责研发这些无人机的风行者公司表示，该款无人机能够在大雾天气飞行，其排放量比同类有人驾驶飞行器减少30%。

11
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:17,990
And in Coventry in the UK, construction has started on an air hub, which will act as a base for police and delivery drones.
此外，在英国考文垂市，一个航空枢纽的建设工程已经启动，这里将成为警用无人机和配送无人机的基地。

12
00:01:17,990 --> 00:01:25,490
Urban-Air Port Limited is working with car-maker Hyundai on the mini-airport, known as a skyport.
城市空中港有限公司正与汽车制造商现代合作打造这座被称为“空中港”的小型机场。

13
00:01:25,490 --> 00:01:30,650
Drones could also play a part in improving the health of millions of people.
无人机还能为改善数百万人的健康状况贡献力量。

14
00:01:30,650 --> 00:01:35,480
In Zanzibar, for example, they’re being used to spray wetlands against malaria.
例如在桑给巴尔，无人机被用于在湿地喷洒药剂，防控疟疾。

15
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:44,560
And writing for BBC Future website, Harriet Constable describes an incredible development project by the University of South Australia.
哈里特·康斯特布尔在为BBC未来频道撰稿时，介绍了南澳大利亚大学一个令人瞩目的研发项目。

16
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:53,580
The plan is for drones to eventually be able to survey populations for disease by reading the blood oxygen levels of humans from the air.
该项目计划让无人机最终能够从空中读取人体的血氧水平，以此对人群进行疾病筛查。

17
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:59,200
They’ll also be able to scan for other vital signs, like coughing and a high temperature.
无人机还将能够侦测咳嗽、高烧等其他生命体征。

18
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:03,630
It seems the sky’s the limit for what drone technology can achieve.
无人机技术的发展潜力似乎无穷无尽。

19
00:02:03,630 --> 00:02:07,700
The only thing that sometimes keeps it grounded is regulation.
有时唯一制约它发展的因素就是监管政策。

20
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:17,830
Writing for the BBC, Jessica Brown says: “If our skies are to become as crowded as our streets, airspace rules need updating to prevent accidents.”
杰西卡·布朗在为BBC撰稿时表示：“若想让天空变得像街道一样繁忙，就必须更新空域管理规则，以避免事故发生。”

21
00:02:17,830 --> 00:02:21,140
There are also related problems, such as noise pollution.
此外，无人机还存在噪音污染等相关问题。
